1. PURPOSE AND DEFINITIONS

The source is published so that anyone can inspect how tokenstat handles data,
contribute improvements, share source changes, and build and run their own
versions.

"Software" means the material covered by section 2, including copies,
modifications, derivative works, and portions of that material. "You" means
the person or entity exercising permissions under this licence.

"Source Form" means the preferred form for making modifications, including
human-readable source code, documentation, configuration and build scripts.

"Build" means a compiled, packaged or otherwise prepared executable version
of the Software, or a product containing such a version, including binaries,
libraries, installers, app bundles, APKs, IPAs, container images, firmware,
and compiled or obfuscated web applications. This includes modified versions
and products incorporating only part of the Software. An archive of Source
Form is not a Build merely because it includes scripts that can be run by an
interpreter. Adding source files to a Build does not make it Source Form.


